# This working tree is shared between macOS and Windows checkouts, so line
# endings must not depend on whichever device last wrote a file.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true rewrites checked-out
# files to CRLF, and every tracked file can then read as locally modified.
#
# LF everywhere also keeps bin/*.sh and the doctor scripts runnable, and lets
# patches/*.patch apply cleanly with `git apply` (which is whitespace-sensitive).
#
# text=auto rather than a blanket `text` so a binary added later is detected and
# left alone instead of being corrupted by newline translation.
* text=auto eol=lf
